whetstone (ccplugins) — sharpen the thinking before the work.

The `/ws:grill` skill is adapted, with modifications, from MIT-licensed prior
work:

  • mattpocock/skills (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Matt Pocock) — the `grilling`
    skill. The design-tree framing, the frontier (every decision whose
    prerequisites are settled), the round structure with the whole frontier
    asked at once, the ❓/➡️ question format with a recommended answer attached
    to every question, the facts-are-the-agent's / decisions-are-the-user's
    split, and the frontier-is-empty completion criterion all originate there.

Unlike a clean-room re-implementation, this is a close textual adaptation: the
skill's prose derives from the original and was rewritten, restructured and
extended rather than re-derived. Modifications are documented in CHANGELOG.md
and cover carrier selection (`AskUserQuestion` versus markdown), the
frontier-before-carrier ordering, enforced non-consent-by-silence with an open
list, and named hand-offs to the other plugins in this marketplace.

